   "title": "Troubleshooting Backup Verification Failures on Attribution Engine",
   "content_summary": "Addresses backup verification failures caused by disk space exhaustion or infrastructure hardware faults on the Attribution Engine. Includes steps for capacity expansion and failover procedures.",
   "content_body": "1. Check the storage volume usage; if near 100%, the verification job will fail due to insufficient write space. 2. Review the database error logs to distinguish between simple capacity limits and underlying hardware I/O errors. 3. For capacity issues, increase the allocated disk space for the backup partition and re-run the verification. 4. If hardware failure is suspected (e.g., SMART errors or persistent timeouts), execute a failover to the standby replica. 5. Schedule replacement of the faulty storage infrastructure immediately after failover."
